1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,669
<i>Three? That's a lot.</i>

2
00:00:02,752 --> 00:00:04,796
<i>This one's for Sir Eric.</i>

3
00:00:04,879 --> 00:00:06,089
[BILLY] <i>Sir Eric?</i>

4
00:00:06,172 --> 00:00:08,675
<i>The parents really love our healthy meals.</i>
<i>They're so happy about them.</i>

5
00:00:08,758 --> 00:00:09,968
<i>Good morning, Ms. Lucy.</i>

6
00:00:10,051 --> 00:00:12,011
[LUCY]<i> Good morning!</i>
<i>Good morning, Oliver!</i>

7
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:13,388
[CHARM] <i>She's lying to us!</i>

8
00:00:13,471 --> 00:00:16,182
[BILLY]<i> I reached out</i>
<i>to your last company,</i>

9
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:18,893
<i>and they mentioned that</i>
<i>you were involved in an accident.</i>

10
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:22,355
<i>They said that you died in that fire.</i>

11
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:25,400
[ABI] <i>They thought it was me,</i>
<i>but I wasn't the one who died.</i>

12
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:28,486
<i>- My sister died, not me.</i>
<i>- I cannot hire you.</i>

13
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:30,864
<i>Abi, I need someone I can trust.</i>

14
00:00:30,947 --> 00:00:34,743
[CALOY] <i>Sir Jordan, please forgive me!</i>
<i>I was just following orders!</i>

15
00:00:34,826 --> 00:00:37,495
- [JORDAN] <i>Who gave you those orders?</i>
- [CALOY] <i>Shirley De Leon!</i>

16
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:40,165
<i>She used to be a LoveList employee, right?</i>

17
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:42,375
<i>She's the one who has a grudge</i>
<i>against Ma'am Billy.</i>

18
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:45,462
Um, but-- but…

19
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:46,671
Chief, don't worry.

20
00:00:46,755 --> 00:00:49,424
I-I'm sure LoveFeast is going to be a hit.

21
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:53,928
But it would be better
if we could get testimonials for this.

22
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:55,138
[PAPERS RUSTLING]

23
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:57,432
What about them? Yani and Toni!

24
00:00:57,515 --> 00:01:00,769
A match made by LoveList!
You're now engaged, right?

25
00:01:00,852 --> 00:01:03,730
Oh, yeah! You're a great fit
for LoveFeast!

26
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:06,566
Yani can even save a lot on your wedding.

27
00:01:06,649 --> 00:01:08,318
I'm happy for you guys!

28
00:01:10,195 --> 00:01:14,574
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

29
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:17,160
Shh! Hey, hey, here, here.

30
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:20,330
You need that.
You've been serious since earlier.

31
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:22,916
Is this still about Abi?

32
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:24,834
No.

33
00:01:27,712 --> 00:01:29,088
Billy…

34
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:32,592
If you have a problem,
you know you can tell us, right?

35
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:36,304
Even if it's not about work, it's okay.

36
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:39,307
Remember, we're not just
your team at LoveList.

37
00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:41,226
We're your friends too.

38
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:48,274
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

39
00:01:48,358 --> 00:01:50,944
Someone called me the other day.

40
00:01:51,569 --> 00:01:52,612
Who?

41
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:55,323
My dad.

42
00:02:01,496 --> 00:02:08,128
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

43
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:48,042
You shouldn't have bothered,
but thank you for this.

44
00:02:48,126 --> 00:02:51,254
It's okay. Auntie helped me prepare that.

45
00:02:51,963 --> 00:02:55,133
- "Auntie"?
- My Auntie Precious.

46
00:02:55,216 --> 00:02:56,968
She's the one who takes care
of me and my sister.

47
00:02:57,051 --> 00:03:01,180
She's my godmother,
but she also became my mom.

48
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:03,600
How about your real mother?

49
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:06,769
She's dead.

50
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:09,647
And your father?

51
00:03:10,356 --> 00:03:11,774
He's dead too.

52
00:03:11,858 --> 00:03:16,529
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

53
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:18,781
What about you? Where's your family?

54
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:21,492
Um…

55
00:03:22,368 --> 00:03:24,120
My family's distant from me.

56
00:03:25,163 --> 00:03:27,832
My eldest has her own company now.

57
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:31,294
My youngest is still studying. You know…

58
00:03:32,086 --> 00:03:34,964
He's very smart. Just like you!

59
00:03:35,882 --> 00:03:38,343
How do you know I am smart?

60
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:39,594
Because of that!

61
00:03:40,970 --> 00:03:43,723
You want to study at
the University of Kingsley, right?

62
00:03:43,806 --> 00:03:45,934
Isn't that a school for smart kids?

63
00:03:46,601 --> 00:03:48,895
I used to work in Canada.

64
00:03:48,978 --> 00:03:51,231
There are lots of good universities there.

65
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:54,234
Oh. But I'd rather go to the US.

66
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:57,904
My sister said
our father's grave is there.

67
00:03:59,364 --> 00:04:01,824
I'll get going now, Sir Eric. Bye!

68
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:07,705
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

69
00:04:07,789 --> 00:04:08,665
[TONI GASPING]

70
00:04:08,748 --> 00:04:10,458
My gosh!

71
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:14,087
So many things are happening to you,
yet you don't share anything with us!

72
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:15,672
We weren't able to be with you!

73
00:04:15,755 --> 00:04:19,884
No, it's okay now. It's okay. I fixed it.

74
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:21,844
Chief, you're incredible.

75
00:04:22,428 --> 00:04:26,140
You still handled LoveFeast
despite everything.

76
00:04:27,016 --> 00:04:31,980
Marj, I can't put LoveList aside
just because my dad came back.

77
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:36,651
The company's been doing good.
We cannot lose momentum.

78
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:39,112
What's with you?

79
00:04:39,195 --> 00:04:42,198
We won't abandon LoveList.

80
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:47,161
But, you know,
we can still talk about things.

81
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:49,914
Remember, you're free to feel things.

82
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:53,835
- You are not a robot.
- Mm-hmm, it's okay now.

83
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:55,837
Let's not make a big deal out of it.

84
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,548
I only mentioned it because you asked me.

85
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:00,341
But, don't worry, it's okay now.

86
00:05:00,425 --> 00:05:04,012
No feelings, no distractions.

87
00:05:04,095 --> 00:05:05,722
Let's just focus.

88
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:08,725
But next time, tell us about it, okay?

89
00:05:09,976 --> 00:05:11,853
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

90
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:17,191
Is there a problem?

91
00:05:17,275 --> 00:05:18,818
You guys are all so serious.

92
00:05:18,901 --> 00:05:21,863
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:23,156
Nothing.

94
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:26,200
Nothing. We're okay now. How did it go?

95
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:27,535
It's done.

96
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:30,747
Hey, don't cry.

97
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:36,085
Nah, I'm kidding.

98
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:39,047
Stop sulking. I have news, remember?

99
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:40,673
It's good news!

100
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:45,178
Think about it.
Jordan and Billy will leave us alone.

101
00:05:45,762 --> 00:05:46,596
Right?

102
00:05:46,679 --> 00:05:50,641
You should've seen it. They really
believed Shirley De Leon was my boss.

103
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:52,143
That was your idea, right?

104
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:55,688
You really impress me.
I mean, you found that out!

105
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:57,065
That was smart of you!

106
00:05:58,066 --> 00:05:59,692
And I think your advice is right.

107
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:01,861
I should change my strategy.

108
00:06:01,944 --> 00:06:05,448
I shouldn't be rash. I shouldn't get mad.

109
00:06:05,531 --> 00:06:06,866
I should plan what to do.

110
00:06:06,949 --> 00:06:09,619
I should have backup plans too
if something unplanned happens--

111
00:06:09,702 --> 00:06:10,536
Abi!

112
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:13,081
- [DOOR CLANGING]
- Abi! Abi!

113
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:15,625
Abi!

114
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:18,503
Abi, stop it! Stop! Abi!

115
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:20,046
You said it yourself.

116
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:24,425
You said it-- Just relax!

117
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:27,887
- Don't be rash--
- Why am I treated like this?!

118
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:31,057
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

119
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:33,810
That Billy is so greedy!

120
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,646
She already has everything!

121
00:06:37,396 --> 00:06:39,315
She has money!

122
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:44,362
She has friends! She has a family!

123
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:45,905
I have nothing!

124
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:51,202
All I'm asking for is a job.

125
00:06:51,285 --> 00:06:54,372
A job! I just want a job!

126
00:06:54,455 --> 00:06:56,457
But she can't even give me that?!

127
00:06:57,166 --> 00:06:58,626
Does she want everything for herself?

128
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:00,711
Then fine, it's all hers!

129
00:07:05,133 --> 00:07:07,218
But I'll take all that away from her.

130
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:09,720
I won't leave her with anything.

131
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,265
We'll--

132
00:07:12,765 --> 00:07:13,975
We'll get back at her.

133
00:07:14,058 --> 00:07:16,894
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

134
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:18,312
I'll get back at her.

135
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:21,107
I will get back at her.

136
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:27,447
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

137
00:07:37,707 --> 00:07:42,086
Caloy gave the number he used
to contact Shirley.

138
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:43,337
[BILLY, SKEPTICALLY] Mm?

139
00:07:43,421 --> 00:07:45,131
But, just like what he said,

140
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:47,592
it's unreachable now.

141
00:07:48,676 --> 00:07:51,220
- Hm.
- And you don't believe it.

142
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:52,889
- Mm-hmm.
- Yeah.

143
00:07:53,973 --> 00:07:56,225
Shirley's had an issue with us
for a long time now.

144
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:57,977
Why is she only taking revenge now?

145
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:00,563
You really think
Caloy's telling the truth?

146
00:08:01,272 --> 00:08:03,065
I mean, we can't be sure.

147
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,317
What I did find out

148
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:06,319
is that Shirley's been wanted for years.

149
00:08:06,402 --> 00:08:07,570
She scammed a lot of people.

150
00:08:07,653 --> 00:08:11,365
But why is it that after she stole from us

151
00:08:11,449 --> 00:08:12,492
and got fired from LoveList,

152
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:15,786
she suddenly had the courage
to do all this illegal stuff?

153
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:17,330
- I don't know.
- Hm.

154
00:08:17,413 --> 00:08:20,249
Maybe that's why it's harder
to find her now.

155
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:22,793
However, we still can't confirm it.

156
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:25,963
- Hey, we'll find a way.
- Mm-hmm.

157
00:08:26,047 --> 00:08:28,591
I believe we will.
The truth eventually comes out.

158
00:08:28,674 --> 00:08:29,759
Always!

159
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:31,594
- [JORDAN] Gab?
- [GAB] Yes, sir?

160
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:34,096
- [JORDAN] All systems go.
- [GAB] Okay.

161
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:38,184
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

162
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:45,816
You should try it on your next date.

163
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:46,734
Chief?

164
00:08:46,817 --> 00:08:48,945
The loan check can be collected tomorrow.

165
00:08:49,028 --> 00:08:50,488
Oh, okay. Thank you.

166
00:08:50,571 --> 00:08:52,698
Also, about Ms. Lindsay's contract,

167
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:55,701
please ask the legal team
to have it prepared.

168
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:56,994
Okay.

169
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:59,997
You sound pretty sure we'll have a deal.

170
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:01,874
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY] Claiming it.

171
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:04,710
- I think we have a deal here, Toni.
- [TONI EXCLAIMS]

172
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:07,004
Chief, just give me a call
if you want more food, okay?

173
00:09:07,088 --> 00:09:09,382
Yes, yes. Come on, go home.
It's getting late.

174
00:09:09,465 --> 00:09:10,967
- Bye.
- Bye.

175
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:11,968
Take care.

176
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:14,971
[TONI] You should make your lips darker.

177
00:09:17,098 --> 00:09:18,766
["MAG-ISA LANG AKO"
BY SHANIAH ROLLO PLAYING]

178
00:09:18,849 --> 00:09:20,935
[DEVICE RINGING]

179
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:23,896
<i>Hi, Billy!</i>

180
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:25,690
Hi!

181
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:27,775
Hi Oliver! Hi, Auntie Pres!

182
00:09:27,858 --> 00:09:28,901
How are you guys doing?

183
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:30,736
<i>Let's eat together.</i>

184
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:33,155
Yes, here's my food. Let's eat together.

185
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:54,969
["MAG-ISA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

186
00:09:57,346 --> 00:09:59,807
[NO AUDIBLE DIALOG]

187
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:15,823
["MAG-ISA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

188
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:37,887
["MAG-ISA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

189
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:57,907
["MAG-ISA LANG AKO" CONTINUES]

190
00:11:13,964 --> 00:11:15,424
[MUSIC FADES]

191
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:19,095
[BERNADETTE] <i>That's exactly</i>
<i>my problem, Billy.</i>

192
00:11:19,178 --> 00:11:20,930
<i>I don't know if they're sincere.</i>

193
00:11:21,013 --> 00:11:22,640
<i>I think the timing is pretty odd.</i>

194
00:11:22,723 --> 00:11:25,184
<i>Suddenly, my family wants to reconcile</i>

195
00:11:25,267 --> 00:11:29,855
<i>right after they saw on social media</i>
<i>that I'm marrying a rich guy.</i>

196
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:31,357
I get you.

197
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:34,527
[BERNADETTE] <i>Simon said</i>
<i>I should give them a second chance.</i>

198
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,737
<i>That's why I called here in LoveLine.</i>

199
00:11:36,821 --> 00:11:38,322
<i>We've been fighting about it.</i>

200
00:11:38,406 --> 00:11:41,283
<i>I don't want to invite my family</i>
<i>to our wedding,</i>

201
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:43,452
<i>but Simon says I should.</i>

202
00:11:43,536 --> 00:11:45,704
[BILLY] You know what,
they're your family.

203
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:47,206
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:11:47,289 --> 00:11:49,583
But they're also the source of your pain.

205
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:52,837
I know your fiancé's opinion
is important to you.

206
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,130
But I'll tell you this.

207
00:11:55,131 --> 00:12:00,302
It's really up to you whether you think
they deserve that invite

208
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:01,512
or not.

209
00:12:01,595 --> 00:12:03,556
Second chances are a gift,

210
00:12:04,348 --> 00:12:05,850
not an obligation.

211
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:09,145
Give it when you're ready.

212
00:12:10,312 --> 00:12:12,523
Thank you
for calling LoveLine, Bernadette.

213
00:12:13,941 --> 00:12:15,568
- Cheers, dude.
- Cheers.

214
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:19,613
Do you really believe
what you said earlier?

215
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:21,157
That

216
00:12:22,074 --> 00:12:23,784
second chances could be earned?

217
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:25,953
If this is about Abi…

218
00:12:26,036 --> 00:12:27,830
No. It's…

219
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:30,541
about your dad.

220
00:12:30,624 --> 00:12:32,293
Let me ask you the same thing.

221
00:12:32,376 --> 00:12:34,044
Do you have it in you to forgive?

222
00:12:34,128 --> 00:12:35,504
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

223
00:12:35,588 --> 00:12:36,755
You know what?

224
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:39,717
When my dad left us,

225
00:12:40,342 --> 00:12:42,011
I told myself

226
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:43,888
that if he came back,

227
00:12:45,014 --> 00:12:46,098
I'd be willing to forgive him.

228
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:47,808
He came back.

229
00:12:48,392 --> 00:12:49,351
He came back

230
00:12:50,227 --> 00:12:52,188
to take me away from Grandpa.

231
00:12:52,271 --> 00:12:53,772
- Hmm.
- That doesn't count.

232
00:12:53,856 --> 00:12:56,192
That's how life turned out for us.

233
00:12:57,526 --> 00:13:00,196
Remember when
the Social Welfare Commission

234
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:04,575
was trying to separate Oliver and me?

235
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:07,661
In my head, I was like, "Don't you dare."

236
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:10,164
And then you kidnapped your own brother.

237
00:13:10,247 --> 00:13:12,208
Yes. Not just once.

238
00:13:12,291 --> 00:13:14,627
And who was your partner in crime again?

239
00:13:15,211 --> 00:13:16,545
Hmm.

240
00:13:16,629 --> 00:13:18,380
<i>Have you seen this child?</i>

241
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:19,298
<i>- No.</i>
<i>- No.</i>

242
00:13:22,635 --> 00:13:23,511
<i>They're coming!</i>

243
00:13:24,094 --> 00:13:25,554
<i>They're coming!</i>

244
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:28,974
<i>They didn't see them here.</i>
<i>Come on, let's check over there.</i>

245
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:37,316
[YOUNG JORDAN PANTING]

246
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:40,277
<i>Thanks, dude.</i>

247
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:45,407
You were a great lookout.

248
00:13:45,491 --> 00:13:47,201
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
- Yes.

249
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:49,245
I felt like a superhero.

250
00:13:49,328 --> 00:13:50,496
[BILLY CHUCKLES]

251
00:13:51,372 --> 00:13:55,376
The things we do for the people we love.

252
00:13:55,459 --> 00:13:59,672
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

253
00:13:59,755 --> 00:14:02,091
I'd do anything for Oliver, dude.

254
00:14:03,592 --> 00:14:06,178
Except maybe one thing.

255
00:14:08,138 --> 00:14:09,348
What?

256
00:14:09,431 --> 00:14:10,766
The truth.

257
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,560
Hmm.

258
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:14,895
[MUSIC TURNS SOMBER]

259
00:14:14,979 --> 00:14:16,188
His father.

260
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:19,984
What happens if Oliver learns
the truth about his dad?

261
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:23,529
I got receipts to prove
that he's not only a bad father,

262
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:25,739
but also a bad person.

263
00:14:26,574 --> 00:14:27,575
Wait.

264
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:29,785
Okay.

265
00:14:32,454 --> 00:14:36,166
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

266
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:37,459
Mm-hmm.

267
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:39,753
He came back here

268
00:14:39,837 --> 00:14:42,131
because he was a scammer in Canada.

269
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:44,758
He and his woman got arrested.

270
00:14:44,842 --> 00:14:48,053
So now I'm sure he's back because

271
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:49,555
he wants money.

272
00:14:49,638 --> 00:14:53,350
I'll make sure
he won't get a thing from me.

273
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:54,894
From us.

274
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:59,398
My brother doesn't deserve
to know him as his father.

275
00:14:59,481 --> 00:15:03,360
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

276
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:04,987
[DOORBELL DINGS]

277
00:15:07,448 --> 00:15:13,537
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

278
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:14,914
- [DOORBELL DINGS]
- Dear?

279
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:17,499
Dear?

280
00:15:20,669 --> 00:15:21,545
Dear?

281
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:22,755
[CAR ENGINE HUMMING]

282
00:15:22,838 --> 00:15:24,340
[ENRICO] Let's talk!

283
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:25,841
Dear!

284
00:15:28,093 --> 00:15:29,178
[DOORBELL DINGS]

285
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:33,098
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

286
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:35,059
[ENRICO] Please, let's talk!

287
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:38,562
[ENRICO] Please, let's talk.

288
00:15:40,689 --> 00:15:43,400
[DOORBELL DINGS]

289
00:15:43,484 --> 00:15:44,902
What are you doing here?

290
00:15:49,156 --> 00:15:50,157
Dear…

291
00:15:50,699 --> 00:15:52,826
Let's talk. Please?

292
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:56,121
We already did. Wasn't that enough?

293
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:58,374
Dear, just please hear me out.

294
00:16:07,758 --> 00:16:09,969
- I can--
- Don't drag us into your mess.

295
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:12,638
I can explain.

296
00:16:12,721 --> 00:16:16,058
Dear, I've made a lot
of bad decisions in my life.

297
00:16:16,141 --> 00:16:17,935
And I want to make them right this time.

298
00:16:21,188 --> 00:16:22,773
T-There's something you should know.

299
00:16:23,399 --> 00:16:24,400
No.

300
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:27,027
You're the one who should listen to me.

301
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:31,865
If you do this again,
I will file a restraining order.

302
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:34,159
I don't want any trouble,

303
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:38,330
but if you drag me into this,
my company, and especially Oliver,

304
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:43,669
I'll find a way
to have your case in Canada reopened.

305
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:48,507
Please, I don't want us to go there.

306
00:16:54,638 --> 00:16:56,015
Leave.

307
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,144
Please.

308
00:17:00,227 --> 00:17:07,234
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

309
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:19,455
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

310
00:17:22,249 --> 00:17:23,792
[OLIVER YAWNS]

311
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:27,171
[OLIVER] Billy?

312
00:17:32,426 --> 00:17:33,469
[BILLY] Hmm?

313
00:17:34,678 --> 00:17:35,721
Hey.

314
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:39,266
Why are you still up?

315
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:42,227
I overheard you arguing with someone.

316
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:44,063
Oh, no, it was nothing.

317
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:46,273
I was just talking to the security guard.

318
00:17:46,356 --> 00:17:47,733
- Sorry.
- That's it?

319
00:17:47,816 --> 00:17:49,526
Go back to bed now. I'll head up in a bit.

320
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:50,652
- Okay.
- Okay.

321
00:17:50,736 --> 00:17:52,112
- Good night.
- Good night.

322
00:17:52,196 --> 00:17:58,410
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

323
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:06,543
[VEHICLE APPROACHING]

324
00:18:06,627 --> 00:18:08,128
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [HORN HONKING]

325
00:18:08,879 --> 00:18:09,963
[DRIVER] Seriously, dude?

326
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:11,340
Do you have a death wish?!

327
00:18:11,423 --> 00:18:13,175
[ENGINE REVVING]

328
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:19,264
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

329
00:18:19,348 --> 00:18:20,849
- [DOOR OPENS]
- [MUSIC ENDS]

330
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:25,062
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

331
00:18:25,145 --> 00:18:26,980
[DOOR CLOSING]

332
00:18:31,401 --> 00:18:32,444
[PRECIOUS] Billy?

333
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:34,780
[SOFTLY] Hmm?

334
00:18:34,863 --> 00:18:35,864
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

335
00:18:35,948 --> 00:18:37,783
Are you sure

336
00:18:37,866 --> 00:18:39,576
that your father won't trouble you again?

337
00:18:40,619 --> 00:18:42,955
If he comes back,

338
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:45,207
I'll be ready, Auntie Pres.

339
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:46,542
Um…

340
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:49,503
All I'm saying is, Billy…

341
00:18:49,586 --> 00:18:51,755
And please don't take this the wrong way.

342
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:52,923
Maybe…

343
00:18:53,006 --> 00:18:54,550
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

344
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:56,426
…this will never end.

345
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:59,930
It's always going to be like this
if you don't talk to him.

346
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:02,641
You should probably do it.

347
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,018
You expect what, Auntie Pres?

348
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:07,771
That we'll sit down for coffee
and catch up

349
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:09,231
as if nothing happened?

350
00:19:11,733 --> 00:19:14,695
I think it's unfair to me and my brother

351
00:19:14,778 --> 00:19:17,823
if he can just come back into our lives
whenever he pleases.

352
00:19:17,906 --> 00:19:19,241
Billy…

353
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:23,328
Especially now that I know
the things he did in Canada,

354
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:26,039
it's all the more reason Oliver
shouldn't find out

355
00:19:26,123 --> 00:19:27,791
that his father is still alive.

356
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:30,711
[MUSIC BECOMES DRAMATIC]

357
00:19:30,794 --> 00:19:33,088
It's for his own good, Auntie Pres.

358
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:39,011
[MUSIC FADES]

359
00:19:39,094 --> 00:19:41,638
- Oh, stop! You're so annoying!
- [CHUCKLING]

360
00:19:41,722 --> 00:19:43,932
- [VALERIE GIGGLING]
- [MAN] You see these guns?

361
00:19:44,016 --> 00:19:46,101
[MAN CHUCKLING]

362
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:47,936
How long have you been working out?

363
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:49,021
Uh…

364
00:19:49,104 --> 00:19:51,315
Since high school?
It's been ten years now.

365
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:53,025
- [LIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]
- [BOTH GIGGLING]

366
00:19:53,108 --> 00:19:54,443
- [VAL SIGHS]
- [MAN MUMBLES] Oh my God.

367
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:55,485
[JORDAN] Sorry, Val.

368
00:19:55,569 --> 00:19:57,654
Can we settle the bill?
We're about to close.

369
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:59,656
Any last orders?

370
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:02,117
Mmm, no.

371
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:04,828
You? Do you want to drink something else?

372
00:20:04,912 --> 00:20:06,580
- Me, I'm good. Are you good?
- You're good?

373
00:20:06,663 --> 00:20:07,706
- All good?
- Yeah.

374
00:20:07,789 --> 00:20:09,082
- Okay, then.
- Oh…

375
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:11,001
Jordan, this is Kevin.

376
00:20:11,084 --> 00:20:14,671
I'm sure you know him because he's
a famous high-fashion influencer.

377
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:16,381
Like, it's obvious!

378
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:19,509
I love, love, love
his skirt and his style!

379
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:21,094
- [GIGGLES]
- [KEVIN CLEARS THROAT]

380
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:23,305
Just my style?

381
00:20:23,931 --> 00:20:25,933
[VALERIE] And your abs, of course!

382
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:27,059
Fine, your abs!

383
00:20:27,142 --> 00:20:28,227
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

384
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:29,895
[VALERIE] Uh, Kevin?

385
00:20:29,978 --> 00:20:33,148
This is Jordan. Jordan, this is Kevin.

386
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:35,859
- Yo, nice to meet you, bro.
- You too.

387
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:36,985
[KEVIN CLEARS THROAT]

388
00:20:37,069 --> 00:20:39,947
Um, you know what?
Actually, I think I changed my mind.

389
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:41,740
I feel like having another drink.

390
00:20:41,823 --> 00:20:42,699
[INHALES DEEPLY]

391
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:44,868
[KEVIN] Well, what if…

392
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:47,162
we continue this in my penthouse?

393
00:20:47,246 --> 00:20:49,164
I mean, it's in Rockwell.

394
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:51,291
- So, what do you say?
- Okay, let's go!

395
00:20:51,375 --> 00:20:53,460
- Sounds good? Let's go!
- Let's go!

396
00:20:53,543 --> 00:20:56,088
Uh, keep the change, and… thanks.

397
00:20:56,171 --> 00:20:57,130
Yeah, let's go!

398
00:20:57,214 --> 00:20:58,799
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

399
00:20:58,882 --> 00:20:59,967
Come on.

400
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:01,426
- Ladies first.
- [GIGGLES]

401
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:04,888
[BOTTLES CLINKING, THUDDING]

402
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:06,848
Fashion influencer?

403
00:21:06,932 --> 00:21:08,642
Oh, come on. That's her bestie.

404
00:21:08,725 --> 00:21:11,103
- [JORDAN SNICKERS]
- Can we not be judgmental?

405
00:21:11,186 --> 00:21:13,313
He was wearing a skirt.

406
00:21:13,397 --> 00:21:14,898
That's called a men's skirt.

407
00:21:14,982 --> 00:21:17,317
Just because he likes fashion
doesn't mean he's gay.

408
00:21:17,401 --> 00:21:18,527
Just admit that you're jealous.

409
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:19,653
Jealous?

410
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:21,571
You like Val?

411
00:21:22,239 --> 00:21:24,032
- Do you?
- No-- I'm busy.

412
00:21:24,116 --> 00:21:25,158
[JORDAN CHUCKLES]

413
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:29,746
[PHONE RINGING]

414
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:31,540
Hello, dude.

415
00:21:31,623 --> 00:21:33,750
I just don't understand Auntie Pres.

416
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:37,087
She knows exactly what
my brother and I went through.

417
00:21:37,170 --> 00:21:39,798
Yet, she chooses to side with my father?

418
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:42,634
She's just really nice.

419
00:21:42,718 --> 00:21:44,928
So, what? Am I the bad guy now?

420
00:21:45,012 --> 00:21:46,763
No.

421
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:49,766
I mean, she's understanding.

422
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:51,351
She's soft…

423
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:53,186
Hearted?

424
00:21:53,270 --> 00:21:54,771
Well, I'm not.

425
00:21:54,855 --> 00:21:55,731
Same.

426
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:58,775
Look, if my dad ever came back,

427
00:21:58,859 --> 00:21:59,901
I would do the same.

428
00:21:59,985 --> 00:22:01,570
This ends here.

429
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:04,239
If the restraining order fails,

430
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:07,242
I'll find a way to drag him
back to prison.

431
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:13,457
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

432
00:22:30,932 --> 00:22:34,102
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

433
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:35,312
[PHOTO FLAPS]

434
00:22:43,445 --> 00:22:45,072
[MARIELA] <i>You don't</i>
<i>stay long in your jobs.</i>

435
00:22:45,155 --> 00:22:46,907
<i>That's why</i>
<i>you won't get anywhere.</i>

436
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:48,533
[ABI] <i>I'll be just like her.</i>

437
00:22:48,617 --> 00:22:50,452
<i>So you won't remind me</i>

438
00:22:50,535 --> 00:22:52,037
<i>that it should have been</i>
<i>me who died.</i>

439
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:54,790
<i>Legally, he's prohibited</i>
<i>from approaching.</i>

440
00:22:54,873 --> 00:22:56,083
<i>Boring!</i>

441
00:22:56,166 --> 00:22:58,001
<i>We have to be</i>
<i>a hundred steps ahead!</i>

442
00:22:58,085 --> 00:23:00,837
<i>So turning</i>
<i>meaningful connection</i>

443
00:23:00,921 --> 00:23:02,506
<i>into lifelong commitments.</i>

444
00:23:02,589 --> 00:23:05,717
<i>But, apparently, it's a replica</i>
<i>of an existing concept.</i>

445
00:23:05,801 --> 00:23:07,219
<i>Somebody leaked the concept?</i>

446
00:23:07,302 --> 00:23:09,054
<i>I'm on my way to Pebblng.</i>

447
00:23:09,137 --> 00:23:10,931
<i>So she wasn't just smart in school.</i>

448
00:23:11,014 --> 00:23:12,349
<i>She was also a thief.</i>

449
00:23:12,432 --> 00:23:15,310
<i>She can't do to me again</i>
<i>what she did before.</i>
